pe/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320938} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e19b52-3f0a-514a-949d-3b9f7f1a85df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320939} {:answer/id #uuid "e34e844e-4158-52a9-8dfc-c027c1164ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320940} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0152b9-87c9-565e-bd4f-bbe5ecd23e60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320941} {:answer/id #uuid "8f16a92a-12a7-5ad9-8af9-086acdab305c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4e19b52-3f0a-514a-949d-3b9f7f1a85df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320939} :answer-field/id #uuid "1abd4a6f-40c6-52a4-8941-88948c541b12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6fdc213-2110-583b-a8c6-53418eb2942c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130767" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(X)=28.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{1}$ and ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+(-7){R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+(-7){R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{1}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{3}{4},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{3}{4}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we only have to multiply the determinant by $\\frac{3}{4}.$ Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =\\frac{3}{4}det(X) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ef071c-45bb-574a-b070-807c7dd9e969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320945} {:answer/id #uuid "c3010179-1f14-5a58-9918-05b8a9cbc830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320946} {:answer/id #uuid "a457a7ac-dec6-550e-a680-061a75d74aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320947} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7fb5ec-85b1-5b85-88ae-8b2c8d1df21b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320948} {:answer/id #uuid "28866ee3-9935-53e1-ab5e-952abbad069f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25ef071c-45bb-574a-b070-807c7dd9e969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320945} :answer-field/id #uuid "3905e9dd-e5e1-5a9e-bc53-d4352b5071f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e978465-6e4c-5a82-bd36-a67c7ca6a448" :question/math-academy-id "q-130843" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbbeb3b9-a41e-523b-a55e-489a23f36710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320952} {:answer/id #uuid "2b6ee52e-6fba-553e-8916-4b66a157cb2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320953} {:answer/id #uuid "dea1b75d-36ee-584c-b4e0-6479448f4fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320954} {:answer/id #uuid "69adc6b5-b138-501f-b9a8-0c0f22eafe08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320955} {:answer/id #uuid "b3b31131-7130-5ff9-87cb-4cf4a1722d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b6ee52e-6fba-553e-8916-4b66a157cb2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320953} :answer-field/id #uuid "163259ce-93e5-5d0d-b2ae-8a745e048783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "118d7900-31be-52e8-afe5-735eec11cee7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130854" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890be7e4-f4c9-5c96-bdb5-907d133c3a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}↔R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118558} {:answer/id #uuid "bb30654d-6dbd-5a98-9d7b-f56d8c76ab08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118559} {:answer/id #uuid "be284e31-2dec-58ef-a1b4-ba706b77a7e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}:=R_{3} + 2R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118560} {:answer/id #uuid "09554b64-dd0c-576e-8398-8157325d10c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-2)R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118561} {:answer/id #uuid "54b8f081-9585-57a6-817e-520d97437321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}R_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09554b64-dd0c-576e-8398-8157325d10c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-2)R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118561} :answer-field/id #uuid "31331c92-5912-5c03-8535-61333df19ca6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d4250d6-4c9c-5a2c-ac92-71ea5c8419b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42076" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3f9788b-1f95-5a17-b2d8-a14f2cb86bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320959} {:answer/id #uuid "71ebcb6a-6ad2-50ec-991a-6ffdcee8ba00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320960} {:answer/id #uuid "7764ad52-4f5d-5e15-b2b9-4fcea5e0a0b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320961} {:answer/id #uuid "c36b7030-17b6-56b1-9052-e5aeb072661a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320962} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d9a06c-27ec-5fd4-b456-b471c420bc75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71ebcb6a-6ad2-50ec-991a-6ffdcee8ba00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320960} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e83c8bc-a042-5278-88eb-03d7f841abca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9b120ee-5bc1-5f2f-b328-9157915a7496" :question/math-academy-id "q-42204" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=4.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\nTherefore, we only have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(4) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b7201c2-9df7-5a26-a1ee-15c35730c006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320966} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c94adb-b68f-5aca-ad5b-fb1b07b0971d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320967} {:answer/id #uuid "36e54bfd-ab88-512c-b6f2-2e5a2195b9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320968} {:answer/id #uuid "a22c9f41-bb6e-59b0-9a69-cf69db041382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320969} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c6bf63-d786-59b9-a671-fabc0ae3d439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36e54bfd-ab88-512c-b6f2-2e5a2195b9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320968} :answer-field/id #uuid "81b33c1e-1b28-5af7-94f6-a607aabf8306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a48d027-d89f-50f3-941c-570bc10f094d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42501" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f11b223-edd2-59b8-b761-164d56e29746" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Row by a Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01af31e1-f39d-5d7e-ba2e-ddaa58ea7af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320973} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6618ee-ed42-5e85-8308-2fba582e7963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320974} {:answer/id #uuid "aa36f530-c828-51d2-94f5-2111cd4ac733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320975} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4d1e66-edf4-5ee5-9e4f-7c1a1d9f4e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320976} {:answer/id #uuid "1bea7e30-b184-5fb7-abb5-844c97993c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01af31e1-f39d-5d7e-ba2e-ddaa58ea7af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320973} :answer-field/id #uuid "47bba02f-4f15-50d7-a7ca-f7edb2945e43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8643d3e8-4b53-50fd-9702-e96c036397cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-42502" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=2.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{3}{2}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1548f75-0eff-5eea-8b46-e55cde11d63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320980} {:answer/id #uuid "9d367593-e2ab-5817-b8cc-6fea2afa470a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320981} {:answer/id #uuid "43db3489-ff1f-5ea0-a124-e7723ae72ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320982} {:answer/id #uuid "4f42c278-df08-5d68-8999-6b3648da8d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320983} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee4e258-49d1-5a49-9cc6-1bddc927f387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1548f75-0eff-5eea-8b46-e55cde11d63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320980} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fa0b0c4-4f81-5062-ae85-deed1cca5e2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a8c8777-953e-5192-986d-746a421489fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-42504" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=5.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{3}:=3{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=3{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $3,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $3$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $3$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =3\\cdot (-det(A)) \\\\  & =-3det(A) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94d0a1cf-04e3-5846-9d7c-1d524a76e697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118630} {:answer/id #uuid "9f59af76-89cd-5337-98b9-11c25feb57bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118631} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c35b4a-d7e4-5562-96bc-47ad22b45940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118632} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e964ce-8c4e-55f5-a76d-5ec41493c38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118633} {:answer/id #uuid "0fdf03b9-553c-56b9-8bc3-4aa41d2a792c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0e964ce-8c4e-55f5-a76d-5ec41493c38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118633} :answer-field/id #uuid "a83d2666-158d-5623-ae88-f7bcdbc660f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5191b0f-c325-5a66-9045-15afd6131a70" :question/math-academy-id "q-42505" :question/problem "Suppose $U$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(U)=10.$ The matrix $V$ is obtained from $U$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+6{R}_{4}$ and ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(V)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+6{R}_{4}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{1}{2},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{1}{2}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we only have to multiply the determinant by $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =\\frac{1}{2}det(U) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f11b223-edd2-59b8-b761-164d56e29746" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Row by a Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf84da04-a57e-5aa0-aa34-5d67f096aa8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118756} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2c640a-080e-5bbe-badf-a18c4608213a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118757} {:answer/id #uuid "00a7a102-ee1d-5be8-8e3a-9f52af436232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118758} {:answer/id #uuid "49cc3b2a-dfda-551a-be8a-ceda702f04a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118759} {:answer/id #uuid "49d75b0d-301d-5223-a20a-d96648e9343e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd2c640a-080e-5bbe-badf-a18c4608213a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118757} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b8e49b0-5573-53ee-8617-4583a47ad748" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d347b77d-0a2e-5499-b039-62abd2cb7bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-43077" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(A)=35.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-\\frac{3}{5}{R}_{1}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-\\frac{3}{5}det(A) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74764043-e1e7-56d6-8f53-9d287a30e538" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Switching Two Rows"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1ded517-8f0d-5d75-8492-1f3fb0fff390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118762} {:answer/id #uuid "e83788e3-f41a-56ca-9885-f70cfd485447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118763} {:answer/id #uuid "35e6392f-b214-5fd8-9f4f-152fbaf8ff19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118764} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6f5444-6094-5c5a-bec0-5cbf8315cd7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118765} {:answer/id #uuid "7338b1ba-7710-5aa1-b0d4-f7dbec6d4de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7338b1ba-7710-5aa1-b0d4-f7dbec6d4de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118766} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e29802-13d5-58d2-a052-d4391f77bb8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccc604d3-9ad8-5639-a449-b6958ef153b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-43078" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(X)=105.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}$ (switching the first and the third rows). What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(105) \\\\  & =-105.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bbf4f4d-cc54-5981-a464-a0d1820f8889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320987} {:answer/id #uuid "8a8366f7-0527-56af-87cf-fd0d62da9232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320988} {:answer/id #uuid "f501f48e-fe9c-514e-a0d4-9dbce25550a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320989} {:answer/id #uuid "41c05df9-aed7-5244-bd6c-465fb11fc2d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320990} {:answer/id #uuid "18125574-295d-56aa-b655-d001daedc864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c05df9-aed7-5244-bd6c-465fb11fc2d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320990} :answer-field/id #uuid "66de77e2-6a67-5092-987b-a9c6939d9f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b507ccf-d3ae-5df6-af42-5488b07aeb4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-43081" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=-108$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by multiplying the $2$nd row by $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nSo, the determinant is multiplied by $-\\frac{1}{2}$ as well.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-108) \\\\  & =54.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74764043-e1e7-56d6-8f53-9d287a30e538" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Switching Two Rows"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5020e525-0314-5fbb-ba0f-176907e8b0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320994} {:answer/id #uuid "399b78ed-d76e-5702-a435-2c1012bbdad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320995} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbd1dd8-8393-55f2-9b15-9d2c1b0d3d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320996} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0815a4-72e4-54de-8d4c-e92a09901b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320997} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4ba22d-761e-557f-bcb7-7c14eea00e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5020e525-0314-5fbb-ba0f-176907e8b0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320994} :answer-field/id #uuid "637ce2ae-dab2-5e38-ae37-fb58300abd6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08ab00c9-14ec-5fe5-8ec6-756810977d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-72716" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(X)=-13.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{2}$ (switching the second and the fifth rows). What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-13) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74764043-e1e7-56d6-8f53-9d287a30e538" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Switching Two Rows"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d06c8ef-9501-5b68-8346-3ce87381c127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "637" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321001} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a1fd04-1a4b-5337-92e2-ed91e746d888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321002} {:answer/id #uuid "f45a96b9-f713-584e-a5b4-e02a41a13537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321003} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb019b5-6ca4-5afc-93a2-a93d761279c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321004} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf61bb1-2dbb-5fbb-a61d-e02aa094d371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f45a96b9-f713-584e-a5b4-e02a41a13537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321003} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ffdf5b3-d6ab-56e3-8a30-c665c4abae51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9eda43c-7621-5b66-9bc7-fe0ed5f28ec0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72723" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $det(B)=91.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{6}↔{R}_{2}$ (switching the second and the sixth rows). What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-det(B) \\\\  & =-(91) \\\\  & =-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f11b223-edd2-59b8-b761-164d56e29746" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Row by a Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e22fb717-af96-5557-849e-60fce14116d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321008} {:answer/id #uuid "a67716a5-79bc-5ad2-bf48-8ad92e65c884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321009} {:answer/id #uuid "354edd58-92ec-51bf-98f9-d529bf75ef45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321010} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e40bf8-3a77-596b-ba77-7bea65ee0aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321011} {:answer/id #uuid "8543308d-ff7a-5ee6-9b44-4151c773c50e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e22fb717-af96-5557-849e-60fce14116d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321008} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f981e6d-fb71-5561-b482-13dffbaac84e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f2913fd-3340-5219-a5c3-5d7856a5db25" :question/math-academy-id "q-72731" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-64.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{8}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{5}{8}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{5}{8}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-64) \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "272d9a54-ba97-5175-86df-0a78337da7b9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00afca60-08e9-5783-9488-441dd8c7b009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321015} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d94863-9ed3-59f9-b2a3-c0c27bb12128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321016} {:answer/id #uuid "d202a94b-c197-5741-a11b-e679cc341c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321017} {:answer/id #uuid "596b29b4-e258-5a79-a9a2-0279cc8fc651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "176" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321018} {:answer/id #uuid "b8862d08-6dbe-5b72-a5c0-3404fd394ae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "275" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d202a94b-c197-5741-a11b-e679cc341c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321017} :answer-field/id #uuid "91225fe5-9eb5-57f1-9e0a-526c76deaf4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "083a3395-401a-51d3-8ccb-128e7665a1f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72739" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(B)=11.$ What is the value of $det(2B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2B) & ={2}^{5}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =32\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =352.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "272d9a54-ba97-5175-86df-0a78337da7b9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cce2f52-acd5-5bdc-8984-d0d6b04ff405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321022} {:answer/id #uuid "d3237d1e-0647-54d0-8885-120132ff8a4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-243" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321023} {:answer/id #uuid "3c00eee5-81c5-5f80-8494-85561a103397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321024} {:answer/id #uuid "160faef4-dabe-52b8-b703-594fb7f264e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321025} {:answer/id #uuid "3a56367f-f948-5c9f-8fcf-2e8e6e1ba7ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c00eee5-81c5-5f80-8494-85561a103397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321024} :answer-field/id #uuid "1591057b-5e5a-59b5-ac08-29c78afe1b27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "572dba31-125d-59f5-ae11-084a66ccaaa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-72740" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(4Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(4Y) & ={4}^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-192.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d66cf4ad-53ef-5823-bca1-ad8d84c6234a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321029} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb800e7-1e61-5883-ae82-fbd8c8064ac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321030} {:answer/id #uuid "cab8f7ae-7900-59db-a19e-74e4417e4168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321031} {:answer/id #uuid "af29924d-4a04-5112-99fe-b1534f4a2783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321032} {:answer/id #uuid "c4368f9c-2ffa-5e2a-96a0-10416427e6c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af29924d-4a04-5112-99fe-b1534f4a2783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321032} :answer-field/id #uuid "272a99f6-2677-5732-b9d2-95d1dd410019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ed22684-4f17-5f2a-bfb1-58585ef7a3b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72752" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-10.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}$ and ${R}_{4}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{4}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{1}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{1}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{1}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
